summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow-up of chronic problems.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Carolyn Smith is a 49-year-old female who is here for follow-up of her chronic problems.

The patient reports that her osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little bit lately. She primarily notices the pain in her elbows. She has been sitting at a computer at the desk more in the office so she does not know if that has increased flare-ups for that, but she wanted to talk to me about that.

She is right-handed. She notes that she is typing all day versus writing so it flares up in both elbows.

She denies any other joint pain. She notes that she occasionally feels a little bit of numbness in her hands when she is typing for long periods of time. She tries to shake out her arms a little bit to relieve that sensation.

She reports that she has had this history of gout. The last episode she had was about 3 months ago. She had some inflammation of her toe. She denies that she has had any other issues with that. She notes that the medication that I gave her really controlled it and she has not seen a flare-up since.

She is doing well with her psoriasis. She notes that it has been under control as well.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Musculoskeletal: Reports osteoarthritis. Denies other joint pain.
• Neurological: Occasional numbness in her hands.
• Dermatological: Psoriasis under control.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Constitutional: In no apparent distress.
• Neck: No cervical lymphadenopathy.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs, gallops, or rubs. No extra heart sounds.
• Gastrointestinal: Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly.
• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the right elbow: There is edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. There is tenderness and an effusion present. Pain with palpation of the olecranon bursa. Pain with pronation and supination. Pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. No lower extremity edema.

RESULTS

• Autoimmune panel: Within normal limits.
• ESR: Within normal limits.
• Uric acid: Within normal limits.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

• Gout: The patient is doing well. She has not had a flare-up since her last episode. I will continue her on Colchicine 0.6 mg BID as needed for flare-ups.
• Osteoarthritis: The patient is doing well. She is having some flare-ups of her right elbow. I will order an x-ray of the right elbow. I will prescribe Meloxicam 15 mg once a day for the pain and swelling.
• Psoriasis: The patient is doing well. I will continue her on the steroid cream for her scalp.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
