Beverly Johnson is a 24-year-old female who presents for her yearly exam.

The patient reports that she has a history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension. She has been doing well until she started working in a bakery this summer. She has been enjoying her job, but she finds herself snacking a lot during her shifts and eating a lot of desserts. She states that her blood sugars have been elevated because of her diet. She is taking her medications as prescribed. She denies any recent trauma or pain. She reports that she is sleeping well, getting 8 hours of rest per night, and denies any weight loss, fever, or chills. She denies any recent changes in her appetite. She denies any chest pain, palpitations, or syncope. She denies any shortness of breath, wheezing, or cough. She denies any abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting. She denies any headaches, dizziness, or fainting spells. She denies any joint pain or swelling. She denies any rashes or lesions.

