• Constitutional: Denies fevers, chills, or weight loss.
• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain, palpitations, or syncope.
• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath or wheezing.
• Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting.
• Neurological: Denies headaches, dizziness, or fainting spells.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies joint pain or swelling.
• Skin: Denies rashes or lesions.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

