Follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis, and food allergy.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

The patient is a 20-year-old female who presents for a follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis, and food allergy. She was last seen in the office in 04/2020. Due to insurance changes, she was switched from Symbicort to Wixela. She uses Zyrtec in the spring, summer, and fall for seasonal allergy symptoms, which tend to work well. She also has a known peanut allergy, tolerates almonds and cashews.

The patient reports that she has been using Wixela, 250/50 mcg, 1 puff in the morning and 1 puff at night. She uses it once in the morning and once at night. She denies any urgent care or ER visits for breathing over the past year. She has been taking the albuterol inhaler rarely, only before strenuous activity. She is trying to use it less frequently as she is trying to join the military and needs to be able to operate at a certain fitness level without an inhaler. She states that she has been taking it less and less. She uses it 3-4 days per week, either in the morning or at night. She does not use it at other times. She reports that it is working well. She denies any use of prednisone for breathing issues.

The patient reports that she is trying to use her daily inhaler less and less. She can do activities such as walking or going to the grocery store without needing her albuterol. She uses it only for exertional activity. She is trying to use her daily inhaler less and less as she is trying to join the military. She reports that if she can prove that she is capable of these activities without an inhaler, it will make it easier for her to join.

The patient reports that she is currently working on being able to operate at a certain fitness level without her inhaler. She will have a fitness test soon and she is trying to be able to pass without needing to use her inhaler. She has been doing well. She does not use her daily inhaler as much as she used to.

MEDICATIONS

Albuterol Inhaler
Zyrtec 10 mg, as needed
Epipen
Wixela, 250/50 mcg, 1 puff in the morning and 1 puff at night
Alvesco, 80 mcg, 2 puffs twice a day

