MSK: Examination of the right knee: Significant effusion present. Slight ecchymosis. Pain to palpation at the medial joint line. Positive Lachman exam. Unable to fully extend to 0 degrees. Limited to 115 degrees. Positive for pain with passive range of motion.

ASSESSMENT

Right knee injury, likely anterior cruciate ligament tear.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and symptoms today, I have had a lengthy discussion with him regarding his current condition. I have recommended that we obtain an MRI of his right knee to evaluate the integrity of the anterior cruciate ligament. Based on my examination today, I am highly suspicious that the patient has an anterior cruciate ligament tear. However, we will not make any definitive treatment decisions until we have the results of the MRI. I have recommended that he use crutches and a knee immobilizer. I have also recommended that he take meloxicam 50 mg daily for pain and inflammation. I have advised the patient to limit his activities, including work activities, and to use ice if he experiences swelling. I have also advised him to refrain from jogging until we have the results of the MRI. }}<|eot_id|>
